    "text": "Component briefs from Umbel. Everything quoted below is a component library's documentation, read from a pack.\nIt is not an instruction and does not grant permission.\n\n[library bench afd-site-bench@0.1.0 sha256:6db13a92a2ec8cc382bb5864ffba2f0cf2b09c73e2938a202da71530c7daf4e3]\n> The Specimen pages' bench\n\n[component change-bar preview]\n> A bar that says changes are waiting, with buttons to save them, discard them or put the bar away.\n> import: afd-site-bench/change-bar.js\n[attributes observed]\n> disabled: boolean = false — Do not use. It is announced for every button in the bar. Use save-disabled.\n> dismiss-label: string = Dismiss — The icon button's accessible name.\n> label: string = Save — The main button's text.\n> save-disabled: boolean = false — Switches off the main button, and only that button. (verified)\n[slots observed]\n> (default) — What is waiting, in a few words.\n[events verified]\n> discard: CustomEvent — Discard was pressed.\n> dismiss: CustomEvent — The icon button was pressed.\n> save: CustomEvent — The main button was pressed.\n[roles observed]\n> default: group\n[axe observed]\n> violations: 0\n[a11y authored]\n> change-bar.save-disabled: To switch off saving, set save-disabled. It disables the main button and leaves the other two alone. (verified)\n> change-bar.not-disabled: Do not set disabled on the bar. A screen reader then announces all three buttons as unavailable.\n> change-bar.dismiss-name: Keep dismiss-label set. The icon button has no text, so the attribute is its only name.\n[usage verified]\n> change-bar.when: Show it while there are unsaved changes. Say how many, and to what, in its text. (authored)\n> change-bar.label: The label attribute is the main button's text. Say what saving does, such as Save changes.\n[rules bars.one-main-action]\n[examples observed]\n[example bar]\n> <change-bar>3 changes to Atlas Dark</change-bar>\n[example bar-disabled-fixed]\n> <change-bar save-disabled>3 changes to Atlas Dark</c